    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Stewards can now reopen a closed period, and all 4 tests in `bin/e2e` pass.\n\n**Server:** I added a `POST /api/sheets/{sheetId}/periods/{name}/reopen` endpoint (`reopen.POST.yml`). It loads the period, then `ReopenPeriod` checks two things:\n- **Steward only:** anyone else is refused with \"Only a steward can reopen a period.\"\n- **Closed only:** reopening a period that is already open is refused with \"The period \u2026 is not closed.\"\n\nEither refusal is a 400 and writes nothing. If both checks pass, the period is marked open again and its stored closing total is cleared, using the existing columns. No database migration was needed. Then the endpoint writes `PERIOD_REOPENED sheet=<id> by=<user> period=<name>` to the audit file.\n\n**Front end:** each period row in `Periods.tsx` now has a Reopen button (`period-reopen`). A refused close or reopen shows the row's `period-error`, and either button clears it the next time it's pressed. After reopening, the row's due-total is worked out live again, so a claim tied to a statement counts at that statement's figure and the rest at today's rates. In the test that gives 11.00 instead of the 6.00 it was closed at.\n\nClaims dated in a closed period already showed their current figures before this change, so nothing needed fixing there.",
